; case: context-save-layout
; verdict: reject
; ambiguous: no
; tests: externality=pass implementation-independence=pass non-prescription=fail
; failing-test: non-prescription
; rationale: Prescribes the register save order and frame shape. §8.2 generates context
;   layouts "from explicit contracts" inside the engine; the ABI, stack policy and nesting
;   rules are engine inputs, not description content. Like `atomic-read-retry-loop`, this case
;   is written WITHOUT an `implementation` wrapper: a layout smuggled in as an ordinary clause
;   is the realistic shape, and the one a classifier has to catch on its own merits.
; other-side: belongs in engine knowledge: the architecture substrate's context layout,
;   derived from the selected ABI and privilege rules
;
(defpolicy task.context
  (save-order (ra sp gp tp t0 t1 t2 s0 s1))
  (frame-align 16 byte))
